Feature: Metallic Industrial Design System
  As a founder, CTO, or engineer viewing the site or tablet kiosk in San Francisco
  I want to experience an interface styled like a precision-engineered physical instrument with tactile 3D depth
  So that the craftsmanship communicates elite technical mastery and authority with zero load-time lag

  Scenario: Apply machined metal tokens and anisotropic brushed gradients
    Given the stylesheet modern-craft.css is loaded
    When inspecting the design system tokens
    Then it should define base metals for gunmetal, space titanium, and brushed steel
    And it should provide CNC chamfer edge highlights reflecting ambient light
    And it should define metallic anodized green as the hero accent and scorched titanium violet for KMP

  Scenario: Style hero CTA button as an anodized green aluminum billet
    Given the visitor views the hero section
    When inspecting the primary action button
    Then it should display as a machined anodized green aluminum block with directional metallic sheen
    And it should feature a specular top edge highlight and tactile pressed depth

  Scenario: Transform Bento Grid into modular titanium rack bays with laser-etched metadata
    Given the Proof of Work Bento Grid is displayed
    When inspecting the project cards
    Then each card should render as a titanium rack bay with subtle CNC bevels
    And each module should display stamped/laser-etched console metadata tags
    And KMP badges should feature scorched titanium metallic violet accents

  Scenario: Implement procedural 3D tilt and anisotropic light with zero asset weight
    Given interactive Bento cards and primary buttons
    When the user interacts via pointer, hover, or touch
    Then the card should smoothly tilt along X and Y axes using hardware-accelerated CSS 3D perspective
    And a dynamic specular highlight gradient should track the pointer across the metallic surface
    And the implementation must require zero raster image sequences or heavy 3D loaders (total transfer < 40 KB)

  Scenario: Style tablet kiosk as a physical titanium diagnostic tool
    Given the tablet kiosk is rendered at /display
    When viewing the full-screen interface
    Then it should render with a physical machined metal bezel and telemetry dot-matrix texture
    And the vector SVG QR code should be framed on a high-purity alloy plate with 45-degree chamfered corners
